@startuml codeemb-codet5
' CodeT5+ embed_code path: optional language prefix, tokenize+truncate, ONNX run,
' rank-dispatch on the output tensor (rank 2 pass-through, rank 3 mean-pool),
' L2 normalize, cache. Muted nodes are configured-but-off by default.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-codet5.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/codet5.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title CodeT5+ — CodeT5Embedder::embed_code (Salesforce/codet5p-110m-embedding)

rectangle "**(code c, language ℓ)**" as q #EF6C00

rectangle "**CodeEmbeddingCache**\nkey = h(c, ℓ)" as cache #00838F

rectangle "**Language prefix**  (off by default)\nuse_language_prefix ∧ ℓ ≠ Unknown\n⇒ input = \"⟨rust⟩ \" ++ c" as pre #90A4AE

rectangle "**Tokenizer**\nencode(input, add_special_tokens = true)\nthen hard truncate to max_length = 512" as tok #EF6C00

rectangle "**ONNX encoder**  (110M params)\nT5 encoder + contrastive projection\ninput_ids · attention_mask" as enc #2E7D32

rectangle "**Rank dispatch**" as disp #388E3C
rectangle "rank 2 → [1, 256]\nthe export already pooled" as r2 #43A047
rectangle "rank 3 → [1, L, d]\n**mean-pool** over L" as r3 #43A047
rectangle "otherwise →\nError::Inference" as rx #90A4AE

rectangle "**L2 normalize**  (normalize = true)" as norm #2E7D32
rectangle "**v̂ ∈ ℝ²⁵⁶**" as out #455A64

q --> cache : probe
cache --> pre : miss
pre --> tok
tok --> enc : (ids, mask)
enc --> disp
disp --> r2
disp --> r3
disp --> rx
r2 --> norm
r3 --> norm
norm --> out
norm -[#00838F,dashed]-> cache : insert
cache --> out : hit

note bottom of enc #E8F5E9
  d is **not** auto-detected: ort 2.0 exposes no
  output-shape inspection, so ""embedding_dim""
  falls back to ""config.embedding_dim"" (Some(256)
  from ""codet5p_110m_embedding"", else 256).
end note

note right of pre #ECEFF1
  CodeT5+ is the **only** shipped embedder that
  can emit a language prefix — and ""use_language_prefix""
  defaults to **false**, so it is off unless you set it.
end note

@enduml
